msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Migrating from GPU to NPU\n"
"\n"
"This guide explains how to migrate an existing GPU-based training script to an NPU (Ascend 910B). Since MindSpore supports both GPU and Ascend backends, most code can run directly on the NPU without modification. However, due to differences in hardware architecture and operator implementation, some code may need adjustments. This guide will help you complete the migration quickly.\n"
"\n"
"## 1. Basic Process\n"
"\n"
"The basic process for migrating from GPU to NPU is as follows:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Check the running environment**: Confirm that the NPU driver and CANN toolkit are installed correctly.\n"
"2. **Modify the running configuration**: Set the target device to `Ascend`.\n"
"3. **Check operator support**: Verify whether the operators used in the model are supported on the NPU.\n"
"4. **Adjust data processing**: Optimize the data processing pipeline for the NPU.\n"
"5. **Debug and optimize performance**: Use profiling tools to identify and resolve performance bottlenecks.\n"
"\n"
"## 2. Environment Preparation\n"
"\n"
"### 2.1 Check the NPU Environment\n"
"\n"
"Before starting the migration, confirm that the following components are installed:\n"
"\n"
"- NPU driver (e.g., Ascend 910B driver)\n"
"- CANN toolkit (e.g., CANN 6.3 or later)\n"
"- MindSpore Ascend version (e.g., MindSpore 2.2.0 or later)\n"
"\n"
"You can check with the following command:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npu-smi info\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the NPU information is displayed correctly, the NPU environment is ready.\n"
"\n"
"### 2.2 Set the Device\n"
"\n"
"In the training script, set the target device to Ascend:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import mindspore as ms\n"
"ms.set_context(device_target=\"Ascend\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If you need to specify a specific NPU device, you can use:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"ms.set_context(device_target=\"Ascend\", device_id=0)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 3. Common Code Modifications\n"
"\n"
"### 3.1 Data Type Modifications\n"
"\n"
"NPU has different support for data types compared to GPU. Common issues include:\n"
"\n"
"- **FP16 support**: The Ascend 910B has strong FP16 support, but some operators may have precision differences.\n"
"- **INT8 support**: Some operators may not support INT8 on the NPU.\n"
"- **Mixed precision**: It is recommended to use MindSpore's automatic mixed precision feature.\n"
"\n"
"Example of mixed precision:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from mindspore import amp\n"
"\n"
"# Enable automatic mixed precision\n"
"model = amp.auto_mixed_precision(model, amp_level='O2')\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3.2 Operator Replacement\n"
"\n"
"Some operators may not be supported or may have poor performance on the NPU. Common replacement suggestions:\n"
"\n"
"| GPU Operator | NPU Replacement | Reason |\n"
"|------------|----------------|------|\n"
"| `nn.Conv2d` | `nn.Conv2d` | Supported, but may need to adjust the layout |\n"
"| `nn.BatchNorm2d` | `nn.BatchNorm2d` | Supported, but may need to adjust the epsilon value |\n"
"| `F.adaptive_avg_pool2d` | `nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d` | Recommended to use the `nn` interface |\n"
"| `F.interpolate` | `nn.ResizeBilinear` | Recommended to use the `nn` interface |\n"
"\n"
"### 3.3 Memory Management\n"
"\n"
"NPU memory management differs from GPU:\n"
"\n"
"- **Memory pool**: The NPU uses a memory pool management mechanism, which may require additional memory configuration.\n"
"- **Memory release**: It is recommended to use `ms.ops.free` to release memory promptly.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import mindspore as ms\n"
"from mindspore import ops\n"
"\n"
"# Release memory promptly\n"
"ops.free()\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3.4 Data Processing Modifications\n"
"\n"
"Data processing on the NPU may require the following adjustments:\n"
"\n"
"- **Use the `mindspore.dataset` API**: It is recommended to use MindSpore's built-in data processing APIs, which have been optimized for the NPU.\n"
"- **Adjust the number of data processing threads**: The NPU may require more data processing threads to fully utilize its computing power.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import mindspore.dataset as ds\n"
"\n"
"# Create a data pipeline\n"
"dataset = ds.ImageFolderDataset(data_path, num_parallel_workers=8)\n"
"dataset = dataset.map(operations=transform, num_parallel_workers=8)\n"
"dataset = dataset.batch(batch_size, drop_remainder=True)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 4. Performance Optimization\n"
"\n"
"### 4.1 Use the Profiling Tool\n"
"\n"
"MindSpore provides a profiling tool that can help you identify performance bottlenecks:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import mindspore as ms\n"
"from mindspore.profiler import Profiler\n"
"\n"
"# Enable the profiler\n"
"profiler = Profiler(output_path=\"./profiler_data\")\n"
"\n"
"# Run the training script\n"
"train_model()\n"
"\n"
"# End the profiler\n"
"profiler.analyse()\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 4.2 Common Performance Optimization Suggestions\n"
"\n"
"1. **Use FP16 mixed precision**: Can significantly improve training speed.\n"
"2. **Adjust the batch size**: The NPU has a large memory capacity, so you can try increasing the batch size.\n"
"3. **Use the data sink mode**: Can reduce the overhead of data transfer.\n"
"4. **Avoid dynamic shapes**: The NPU performs better with static shapes.\n"
"\n"
"Example of the data sink mode:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"# Use the data sink mode\n"
"model.train(epochs, dataset, sink_size=100)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 5. Common Issues and Solutions\n"
"\n"
"### 5.1 Operator Not Supported\n"
"\n"
"**Problem**: An error message appears saying that a certain operator is not supported on the NPU.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**:\n"
"1. Check the MindSpore operator support list to confirm whether the operator is supported.\n"
"2. Try replacing it with an equivalent operator.\n"
"3. Use the `ms.ops` functional interface instead of the `nn` interface.\n"
"\n"
"### 5.2 Precision Issues\n"
"\n"
"**Problem**: The training results on the NPU differ from those on the GPU.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**:\n"
"1. Check whether the data type settings are consistent.\n"
"2. Try disabling mixed precision.\n"
"3. Adjust the epsilon value of BatchNorm.\n"
"\n"
"### 5.3 Memory Overflow\n"
"\n"
"**Problem**: An error message appears saying that NPU memory is insufficient.\n"
"\n"
"**Solution**:\n"
"1. Reduce the batch size.\n"
"2. Use the memory pool configuration.\n"
"3. Release memory promptly.\n"
"\n"
"## 6. Summary\n"
"\n"
"Migrating from GPU to NPU is usually straightforward, as MindSpore provides good compatibility. Most code can run directly on the NPU, but you may need to adjust operators, data types, and memory management. It is recommended to use the profiling tool to identify performance bottlenecks and optimize accordingly.\n"
"\n"
"If you encounter problems during the migration, refer to the MindSpore official documentation or contact the community for support.\n"

msgid "GPU Triton算子迁移"
msgstr "Migrating GPU Triton Operators"

msgid "概述：本文介绍 GPU Triton 算子迁移到昇腾 NPU 时的通用处理思路和常见问题。迁移时建议先完成 Python 侧设备与运行时接口替换，再检查 grid 分核、访存对齐、单核计算、UB 空间和 coreDim 限制，最后结合具体示例完成代码修改和正确性验证。"
msgstr "Overview: This article introduces the general handling approach and common issues when migrating GPU Triton operators to Ascend NPU. During migration, it is recommended to first complete the replacement of device and runtime interfaces on the Python side, then check grid partitioning, memory access alignment, single-core computation, UB space, and coreDim constraints, and finally complete code modification and correctness verification with specific examples."

msgid "通用迁移流程"
msgstr "General Migration Process"

msgid "迁移 Python 侧设备和运行时接口"
msgstr "Migrate Python-side device and runtime interfaces."

msgid "在修改具体 Triton kernel 前，先完成 Python 侧设备迁移："
msgstr "Before modifying the specific Triton kernel, first complete the device migration on the Python side:"

msgid "在 Python 文件中增加 `import torch_npu`。"
msgstr "In the Python file, add `import torch_npu`."

msgid "查找 `device=\"cuda\"`、`device='cuda'`、`.cuda()` 和 `.to(\"cuda\")` 等设备指定方式，改为 `device=\"npu\"`、`device='npu'`、`.npu()` 或 `.to(\"npu\")`。"
msgstr "Search for device specifications such as `device=\"cuda\"`, `device='cuda'`, `.cuda()`, and `.to(\"cuda\")`, and change them to `device=\"npu\"`, `device='npu'`, `.npu()`, or `.to(\"npu\")`."

msgid "查找 `torch.cuda.*`、CUDA stream、CUDA event、CUDA synchronize 等 GPU 专属接口，改为 NPU 对应接口或删除不必要的同步逻辑。"
msgstr "Search for GPU-specific interfaces such as `torch.cuda.*`, CUDA streams, CUDA events, and CUDA synchronize, and replace them with the corresponding NPU interfaces or remove unnecessary synchronization logic."

msgid "删除只为 GPU 设备发现服务的逻辑，例如 `triton.runtime.driver.active.get_active_torch_device()` 相关设备断言。"
msgstr "Remove logic that only serves GPU device discovery, such as device assertions related to `triton.runtime.driver.active.get_active_torch_device()`."

msgid "保持 Triton kernel 主体逻辑不变，先用 NPU Tensor 完成编译和正确性验证。"
msgstr "Keep the main logic of the Triton kernel unchanged, and first use NPU Tensor to complete compilation and correctness verification."

msgid "调整 grid 分核"
msgstr "Adjust the grid split cores."

msgid "GPU 上常见的写法会把 grid 设计为大量逻辑 program，由硬件和运行时调度到 SM 上执行。迁移到 NPU 时，应优先考虑物理 AI Core 数量和算子类型："
msgstr "Common practice on GPU designs the grid as a large number of logical programs, which are scheduled onto SMs by the hardware and runtime for execution. When migrating to NPU, priority should be given to the physical AI Core count and operator types:"

msgid "grid 优先使用 1D；2D NPU 适配写法也会合并为 1D，例如 `(20,)` 与 `(4, 5)` 的效果相同。"
msgstr "grid prioritizes 1D; the 2D NPU-adapted syntax is also merged into 1D, for example, `(20,)` and `(4, 5)` have the same effect."

msgid "Vector-only 算子的并发任务数通常按 Vector Core 数量组织；包含 `tl.dot` 的算子通常按 AI Core 数量组织。"
msgstr "The concurrency task count for vector-only operators is typically organized based on the number of Vector Cores; operators containing `tl.dot` are usually organized based on the number of AI Cores."

msgid "当逻辑 grid 远大于物理核数时，需要评估是否改成每个 program 内部循环处理多个 tile，或在逻辑核之间无顺序依赖时使用 `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL`。"
msgstr "When the logical grid is much larger than the number of physical cores, it is necessary to evaluate whether to change to a loop inside each program to process multiple tiles, or to use `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL` when there is no sequential dependency between logical cores."

msgid "coreDim 不能超过 `UINT16_MAX`（65535），大 shape 算子需要结合 BLOCK_SIZE 或分块方式控制 grid 大小。"
msgstr "coreDim cannot exceed `UINT16_MAX` (65535). Operators with large shapes need to control the grid size by combining BLOCK_SIZE or a block-based approach."

msgid "维度"
msgstr "Dimension"

msgid "核心结构"
msgstr "Core structure"

msgid "算子类型"
msgstr "Operator type"

msgid "昇腾 NPU (Ascend)"
msgstr "Ascend NPU"

msgid "多个 AI Core，分为 Cube Core（矩阵乘）和 Vector Core（向量计算）"
msgstr "Multiple AI Cores, divided into Cube Core (matrix multiplication) and Vector Core (vector computation)."

msgid "Vector-only 算子 → 并发任务数 = Vector Core 数；含 `tl.dot` 算子 → 并发任务数 = AI Core 数"
msgstr "Vector-only operators → number of concurrent tasks = number of Vector Cores; operators containing `tl.dot` → number of concurrent tasks = number of AI Cores."

msgid "GPU NVIDIA/AMD"
msgstr "NVIDIA/AMD GPU"

msgid "多个 CUDA Core（标量/向量计算） + Tensor Core（矩阵乘）"
msgstr "Multiple CUDA Cores (scalar/vector computation) + Tensor Cores (matrix multiplication)"

msgid "GPU 算子一般由编译器和硬件自动决定并发度"
msgstr "GPU operators generally have their concurrency automatically determined by the compiler and hardware."

msgid "检查单核数据搬运"
msgstr "Check single-core data transfer."

msgid "完成设备替换后，需要继续检查单个 program 内的数据搬运方式："
msgstr "After completing the device replacement, you need to continue checking the data transfer method within a single program:"

msgid "Vector 算子场景下要求 32 字节访存对齐，cube-vector 融合算子场景下要求 512 字节对齐。"
msgstr "In the Vector operator scenario, 32-byte memory access alignment is required; in the cube-vector fusion operator scenario, 512-byte alignment is required."

msgid "保留 tail mask，确认边界元素不会越界访问。"
msgstr "Keep the tail mask, and ensure that boundary elements will not cause out-of-bounds access."

msgid "检查一次 tile 的片上内存占用，避免触发 UB 空间溢出。"
msgstr "Check the on-chip memory usage of a tile once to avoid triggering UB space overflow."

msgid "移除或替换 GPU 专属同步 API，例如 CUDA thread、stream、event 或 kernel synchronize 相关接口。"
msgstr "Remove or replace GPU-specific synchronization APIs, such as CUDA thread, stream, event, or kernel synchronize related interfaces."

msgid "检查单核数据运算"
msgstr "Check single-core data computation."

msgid "NPU 与 GPU 的计算单元和支持的数据类型存在差异。迁移后应先保证正确性，再根据性能问题调整："
msgstr "NPU and GPU differ in their compute units and supported data types. After migration, correctness should be ensured first, and then adjustments should be made based on performance issues."

msgid "对整数索引、offset、长度等中间值，优先确认当前数据类型是否被 NPU 路径高效支持。"
msgstr "For intermediate values such as integer indices, offsets, and lengths, first confirm whether the current data type is efficiently supported by the NPU path."

msgid "对含 `tl.dot` 的算子，确认 M/N/K tile、累加 dtype 和输出 dtype 是否符合 NPU 后端要求。"
msgstr "For operators containing `tl.dot`, confirm whether the M/N/K tile, accumulation dtype, and output dtype meet the NPU backend requirements."

msgid "对长序列、长 hidden size 或大 K 维循环，优先通过 tiling 控制单次搬入和计算规模。"
msgstr "For long sequences, large hidden sizes, or large K-dimensional loops, prioritize controlling the size of each data transfer and computation through tiling."

msgid "迁移示例"
msgstr "Migration Example"

msgid "示例 1：向量加法完整迁移"
msgstr "Example 1: Complete Migration of Vector Addition"

msgid "import torch\\n"
msgstr "import torch"

msgid "示例 2：设备替换与单核数据搬运"
msgstr "Example 2: Device Replacement and Single-Core Data Transfer"

msgid "以下示例展示将设备从 CUDA 替换为 NPU 后，对单核数据搬运场景进行正确性验证："
msgstr "The following example demonstrates correctness verification for a single-core data transfer scenario after replacing the device from CUDA to NPU:"

msgid "import pytest\\n"
msgstr "import pytest"

msgid "常见问题概览"
msgstr "Frequently Asked Questions Overview"

msgid "完成迁移基础步骤后，可能会遇到新的问题，新问题可归纳为以下两类："
msgstr "After completing the basic migration steps, you may encounter new issues, which can be categorized into the following two types:"

msgid "coreDim 限制问题"
msgstr "coreDim limitation issue"

msgid "当网格维度超过NPU硬件限制时触发。 典型错误信息：`coreDim=xxxx can't be greater than UINT16_MAX`。"
msgstr "Triggered when the grid dimension exceeds the NPU hardware limit. Typical error message: `coreDim=xxxx can't be greater than UINT16_MAX`."

msgid "UB 空间溢出"
msgstr "UB space overflow"

msgid "内存使用超出NPU缓存容量。 典型错误信息：`ub overflow, requires xxxx bits while 1572864 bits available!`。"
msgstr "Memory usage exceeds NPU cache capacity. Typical error message: `ub overflow, requires xxxx bits while 1572864 bits available!`"

msgid "解决 coreDim 超限问题"
msgstr "Resolve the coreDim out-of-bounds issue."

msgid "问题分析: NPU的 coreDim 参数不能超过 UINT16_MAX（65535）。当处理大规模数据时，简单的grid划分可能导致该限制被突破。"
msgstr "Problem Analysis: The coreDim parameter of the NPU cannot exceed UINT16_MAX (65535). When processing large-scale data, simple grid partitioning may cause this limit to be exceeded."

msgid "案例：zeros_like 函数优化 数据规模：N = 1073741824，原始 BLOCK_SIZE = 2048，计算得到的 coreDim = 524288 > 65535（超限）"
msgstr "Case: zeros_like function optimization. Data scale: N = 1073741824, original BLOCK_SIZE = 2048, calculated coreDim = 524288 > 65535 (exceeds limit)."

msgid "解决思路1： 昇腾编译器针对coreDim超限问题，有对应的解决方案，只需将环境变量'TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL'设为1。设置命令如下："
msgstr "Solution 1: The Ascend compiler has a corresponding solution for the coreDim limit issue. Simply set the environment variable 'TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL' to 1. The setting command is as follows:"

msgid "export TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL=1\\n"
msgstr "export TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL=1"

msgid "解决思路2： 通过增大 BLOCK_SIZE 来减少所需的核心数量，确保 coreDim 不超过限制。 计算公式如下："
msgstr "Solution Approach 2: Reduce the number of required cores by increasing BLOCK_SIZE, ensuring that coreDim does not exceed the limit. The calculation formula is as follows:"

msgid "coreDim = ceil(N / BLOCK_SIZE)\\n"
msgstr "coreDim = ceil(N / BLOCK_SIZE)"

msgid "代入 `N = 1073741824` 可得："
msgstr "Substituting `N = 1073741824` yields:"

msgid "ceil(1073741824 / 65535) = 16385\\n"
msgstr "ceil(1073741824 / 65535) = 16385"

msgid "因此，如果 `BLOCK_SIZE` 按 2 的幂取值，至少应设置为 `32768`。"
msgstr "Therefore, if `BLOCK_SIZE` is set to a power of 2, it should be at least `32768`."

msgid "优化前的代码："
msgstr "Code before optimization:"

msgid "import logging\\n"
msgstr "import logging"

msgid "优化后的代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "动态计算适合的 BLOCK_SIZE 以避免 coreDim 超限"
msgstr "Dynamically calculate the appropriate BLOCK_SIZE to avoid exceeding the coreDim limit."

msgid "optimal_block_size = 32768  # The optimized value derived from calculation\\n"
msgstr "optimal_block_size = 32768  # The optimized value derived from calculation"

msgid "处理复合问题：coreDim + UB 溢出"
msgstr "Handling composite issues: coreDim + UB overflow"

msgid "问题分析: 在某些情况下，解决了 coreDim 问题后可能引发新的UB溢出问题。这通常发生在增大 BLOCK_SIZE 后，单个线程块需要处理的数据量超出了NPU的UB缓存容量。"
msgstr "Problem Analysis: In some cases, resolving the coreDim issue may introduce new UB overflow problems. This typically occurs when, after increasing BLOCK_SIZE, the amount of data that a single thread block needs to process exceeds the UB cache capacity of the NPU."

msgid "案例： 数据规模：N = 1073741824，原始 BLOCK_SIZE = 4096，计算得到的 coreDim = 262144 > 65535（超限），调整为 BLOCK_SIZE = 32768 后，coreDim = 32768（合规），但出现 UB 溢出"
msgstr "Case: Data size: N = 1073741824, original BLOCK_SIZE = 4096, calculated coreDim = 262144 > 65535 (exceeds limit). After adjusting BLOCK_SIZE = 32768, coreDim = 32768 (compliant), but UB overflow occurs."

msgid "解决思路： 引入 BLOCK_SIZE_SUB 参数，将大块进一步细分，在保持合理 coreDim 的同时控制内存使用。 优化前代码："
msgstr "Solution approach: Introduce the BLOCK_SIZE_SUB parameter to further subdivide large blocks, controlling memory usage while maintaining a reasonable coreDim. Code before optimization:"

msgid "优化后代码："
msgstr "Optimized code:"

msgid "为什么会出现UBSIZE超出内存的错误"
msgstr "Why does the UBSIZE exceed memory error occur?"

msgid "切分不合理,存在过多的非对齐访存或者运算，例如对（64，32）二维数据搬运，对应stride(12832，128),如果是对齐数据的访存，对应的stride(32,1)。对于非对齐访问内容，在最内轴新增一个大小为1的轴，变为（64，32，4）由于硬件要求vector算子场景ub内存32Byte对齐，假设type=float16，对应stride应该为(12832, 128,1)"
msgstr "Poor tiling leads to excessive unaligned memory access or computation. For example, when moving a (64, 32) two-dimensional data block, the corresponding stride is (12832, 128). If it were aligned memory access, the stride should be (32, 1). For unaligned access content, add a new axis of size 1 to the innermost dimension, making it (64, 32, 4). Since the hardware requires 32-byte alignment for UB memory in vector operator scenarios, assuming type=float16, the corresponding stride should be (12832, 128, 1)."

msgid "离散访存代码逐行对比观察scalar低效映射"
msgstr "Let's compare the discrete memory access code line by line to observe the inefficient scalar mapping."

msgid "设置环境变量TRITON_DEBUG=1, 保存~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter，然后执行"
msgstr "Set the environment variable TRITON_DEBUG=1, save ~/.triton/cache/xxx.ttadapter, then execute"

msgid "bishengir-compile xxx.ttadapter --target=Ascend910B3 --enable-auto-multi-buffer=True --enable-hfusion-compile=true --enable-hivm-compile=true --enable-triton-kernel-compile=true --hivm-compile-args=bishengir-print-ir-after=hivm-inject-sync\\n"
msgstr "bishengir-compile xxx.ttadapter --target=Ascend910B3 --enable-auto-multi-buffer=True --enable-hfusion-compile=true --enable-hivm-compile=true --enable-triton-kernel-compile=true --hivm-compile-args=bishengir-print-ir-after=hivm-inject-sync"

msgid "会有输出IR，对比Triton 算子逻辑与IR内部的操作，观察是否有未映射成指令的操作。 观察HIVM IR阶段是否存在纯scalar搬运或者计算，没有映射为simd指令，这会成为性能瓶颈。"
msgstr "There will be output IR. Compare the Triton operator logic with the operations inside the IR to observe whether there are any operations that have not been mapped to instructions. Observe whether there is pure scalar data movement or computation in the HIVM IR stage that has not been mapped to SIMD instructions, as this could become a performance bottleneck."

msgid "问题：离散访存 && scalar低效映射 b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32]  Triton原先写法利用thread的方式 对[1024,32] 中的最低维度32绑定线程块, 再对1024切16，分为[64， 16， 32]，再对64绑定线程块"
msgstr "Problem: Discontinuous memory access && scalar inefficient mapping b[1024, 32] = a[1024, 32] The original Triton implementation uses threads to bind the lowest dimension 32 in [1024, 32] to thread blocks, then splits 1024 into 16, resulting in [64, 16, 32], and then binds 64 to thread blocks."

msgid "chunk_fwd_kernel_o[(NT, B * H)](\\n"
msgstr "chunk_fwd_kernel_o[(NT, B * H)]("

msgid "优化思路"
msgstr "Optimization approach"

msgid "调整 block_ptr 的 shape/stride: 把 (1024, 32) 看成二维矩阵，最低维度 32 是连续的，所以 stride 应该是 (32, 1)，而不是 (32,)，这样每个线程块能访问连续的 32 元素。让线程块绑定到行维度（1024），每个线程处理一整行的 32 元素。这样访存就是连续的，亲和性好。"
msgstr "Adjust the shape/stride of block_ptr: treat (1024, 32) as a two-dimensional matrix, where the lowest dimension of 32 is contiguous, so the stride should be (32, 1) instead of (32,), allowing each thread block to access 32 contiguous elements. Bind the thread block to the row dimension (1024), with each thread processing an entire row of 32 elements. This makes memory access contiguous and improves affinity."

msgid "比如："
msgstr "For example:"

msgid "block_ptr = tl.make_block_ptr(\\n"
msgstr "block_ptr = tl.make_block_ptr("
